  "notes": "Per the 2026-2027 Texas A&M University undergraduate catalog: Biomedical Sciences (BS). Prerequisites are not listed in the catalog's plan of study grid; consult course descriptions.\nCatalog footnotes:\n[grid1 fn1] Common Body of Knowledge Courses (CBK) must be completed with a grade of C or better. All CBK courses must be complete prior to advancing to the third and fourth year upper-division requirements.\n[grid1 fn2] To fulfill the 6-8 hours of core mathematics, students must (i) select one of the following from MATH 142 , MATH 147 , MATH 151 , MATH 171 ; and (ii) select one of the following from MATH 140 , MATH 148 , MATH 150 , MATH 152 , MATH 172 , STAT 201 .\n[grid1 fn3] A minimum of 4 total credits are required. Select from the following: BIMS 110 , VIBS 111 , VIBS 210 , VIBS 222 , VIBS 413 , VTPB 221 , VTPP 330 .\n[grid1 fn4] HIST 105 and HIST 106 are recommended, however students may choose from other American History core courses.\n[grid1 fn5] To fulfill the Anatomy and Physiology Requirement, students must complete one of the following sequences: (i) BIOL 319 , BIOL 320 , and VTPP 413 , or (ii) VIBS 446 or VIBS 402/BIMS 402 , VTPP 423 , and VTPP 427 . Consult an advisor for permissible course sequencing.\n[grid1 fn6] Select any course 100-499 except MATH 102-104; only 1 credit KINE 199 may be used.\n[grid1 fn7] Students who complete STAT 201 in Mathematics core must take STAT 312 .",
